{"team":"PIT","col":"#FFD84D","identity":"balanced","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":59.5,"adot":7.0,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Matchup-Driven</h2><p>Their backs are a real part of the passing game \u2014 RBs see <strong>25%</strong> of targets (vs ~18%), which props up <strong>Jaylen Warren</strong>'s reception floor.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They lean on tempo \u2014 a 18% no-huddle rate (league ~11%) that inflates snap counts and everyone's volume.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 42% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>49%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Jaylen Warren</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 67 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR2s</strong> \u2014 42 rec yds/game (vs ~36). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>114 rushing</strong> and <strong>250 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.39/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Aaron Rodgers","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":5,"props":{"Comp":21.4,"Att":33.02,"Pass Yds":227.47,"Pass TD":1.71,"INT":0.46,"Rush Yds":5.34}},{"name":"Mason Rudolph","slot":"QB2","starter":false,"td":5,"props":{"Comp":3.1,"Att":4.71,"Pass Yds":32.32,"Pass TD":0.18,"INT":0.29,"Rush Yds":5.0}}],"RB":[{"name":"Jaylen Warren","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":25,"props":{"Rush Att":12.72,"Rush Yds":58.65,"Tgt":2.89,"Rec":2.44,"Rec Yds":17